A||||79||Cooter||New intake kicks butt! Pic enclosed.||||1||
Z||000000||Cooter||10-20-2001||05:24 PM||||After seeing how some folks don't even test what they try to sell, I thought that I would build my own custom intake. Before I started this project, I ran the car with the old intake on the G-tech and got 167 horsepower. I finally got the new itake installed today and kind of hooked up (linkage issues  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"> ) and took the same G-tech trip. . .  203 Horsepower! Now, time to tune the chip for even more  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Dcp01686.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000001||gt boy||10-20-2001||06:06 PM||||what in the hell is that?! <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/eek.gif"><P><BR>------------------<BR>"it's too bad he had to run out of talent half way through the corner..."<p>[This message has been edited by gt boy (edited 10-20-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||Gerald||10-20-2001||06:14 PM|||| <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_wtf.gif"> im gonna have to agree wit gt boy. Dat is fuging ugly. but the #'s are nice<P>------------------<BR>87 coupe 5 spd||||reg||1
Z||000003||Joe Torma||10-20-2001||06:19 PM||||Now that is ingenious!!!  Great #s...kinda looks like the USSEnterprise to me for some reason!?!<P>You can make anything look nice by hiding it under a piece of plastic! <P>Hey, did you measure 0-60 increase?<p>[This message has been edited by Joe Torma (edited 10-20-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000004||Cooter||10-20-2001||06:20 PM||||LOL! It is 3.5 inch DOM aluminum pipe welded into a stock center section of the stock manifold with two original throttle bodies. Ugly, yes. But close the hood and away you go!||||reg||1
Z||000005||88formula||10-20-2001||06:44 PM|||| Dual throttle bodies wow! Paint them red.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/88formula_logo_1.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000006||SLYGUY||10-20-2001||06:47 PM||||I hope that it works out well for you, but DAMN that thing is so ugly you could slap it and it would just smile!!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>Sly||||reg||1
Z||000007||Svyn||10-20-2001||07:16 PM||||Neat, I like the idea of trying new things. Awesome #'s out of that too. Do you have any closer pictures or more indepth info ? I am intrigued. Good job.||||reg||1
Z||000008||jelly2m8||10-20-2001||07:29 PM||||I think that looks wild!<P>Looks quite exotic when ya concentrate looking at the dual throttle bodies.<P>NICE WORK!||||reg||1
Z||000009||Formula88||10-20-2001||07:36 PM||||I like it!  The numbers speak for themselves.  I may just try something like that on mine.  Sure - you could play around with it and make it prettier.  Possibly a future project.  Prototypes are rarely pretty.  <P>To have a 167hp baseline, you must be running a modded 3.4, correct?  I wonder what that would do for a stock 2.8?  Did you notice much loss in the low end?  You've greatly increased the plenum volume and shortened the intake runners.  That should tune it for higher rpms.<P>I'm thinking about trying some type of intake with individual trumpet intakes for each cylinder.  More for the exotic look than pure performance, but it has the potential to have even greater performance.  Simply change the length of the velocity stacks to tune the torque curve.  I've seen setups online with port injection, but they are way expensive.  That's the inspriation, though.  ||||reg||14
Z||000010||hugh||10-20-2001||07:52 PM||||Ingenious,to say the least!||||reg||1
